		<h2 id="requirements">Before you start</h2>
		<p>
			You need a Meeko application, Node.js 24 or later and Meeko
			<code>&gt;=1.7 &lt;2</code>. The i18n module ships separately; you can use it with your application's components.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="Terminal"
			bind:code="examples.install"
		/>
		<h2 id="configuration">Configure the module</h2>
		<DocsCode
			label="meeko.config.ts"
			bind:code="examples.config"
		/>
		<p>
			Catalog paths are relative to the project root and must stay inside it.
			<code>defaultLocale</code>
			must name one of the configured languages.
		</p>
		<h2 id="catalogs">Create the catalogs</h2>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/locales/es.json"
			bind:code="examples.catalog"
		/>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/locales/en.json"
			bind:code="examples.englishCatalog"
		/>
		<p>
			Both languages declare the same keys and parameters. The structure of
			<code>cart</code>
			produces the key
			<code>cart.items</code>.
		</p>
		<h2 id="component">Translate in a component</h2>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.usage" />
		<p>
			<code>useI18n</code>
			is auto-imported in components once the module is registered. It also supports an explicit import from
			<code>@meekojs/i18n</code>. The plugin provides one instance per application and SSR request.
		</p>
		<UIAlert tone="info">
			After changing the catalogs, run
